Package: DRBayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Doubly Robust Causal Inference Methods
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shunichiro", "Orihara", role = "aut"),
    person("Tomotaka", "Momozaki", email = "t_momozaki@rs.tus.ac.jp",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Shonosuke", "Sugasawa", role = "aut"))
Description: Bayesian doubly robust estimation of average treatment effects via
    posterior coupling, in which the outcome-model and propensity-score
    posteriors are linked so that the doubly robust moment condition is
    satisfied. Gibbs samplers for linear, logistic and probit models under
    conjugate or horseshoe priors are provided, and posterior draws produced by
    external Bayesian software can be supplied instead. A Bayesian bootstrap
    estimator and utilities for replicated simulation studies are also
    included. The methodology is described in Orihara, Momozaki and Sugasawa
    (2025) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2506.04868>.
